/**
 * Wave 4 games — make ARK: Survival Ascended, Soulmask, Don't Starve Together,
 * Vintage Story, Necesse, Team Fortress 2 and Left 4 Dead 2 orderable. Same
 * Docker/OsTemplate pattern as Waves 1-3: each is a community Docker image
 * (wrapping SteamCMD, +Wine/Proton-GE where the dedicated-server build is
 * Windows-only) installed by the OsTemplate.setupScript in cloud-init.
 * Researched 2026-08-31 against each game's official dedicated-server docs /
 * SteamDB / Docker Hub — all seven have real, currently-shipping dedicated
 * server support.
 *
 * DayZ was researched alongside this batch and is DELIBERATELY NOT SEEDED:
 * its official dedicated server (SteamCMD app 223350) requires a Steam login
 * from an account that actually OWNS DayZ — anonymous SteamCMD login (which
 * every single other family in this entire catalog relies on, baked into a
 * public OsTemplate.setupScript) does not work for it, and that applies to
 * both the server binary and Workshop mods. There is no existing platform
 * mechanism to hold a customer's or Nxeon's own Steam username/password (plus
 * Steam Guard/2FA) for unattended cloud-init provisioning, and building one is
 * a real feature, not a data-seeding task. This is a genuine provisioning
 * blocker, not a "no real dedicated server" case — see lib/games.ts.
 *
 * Steam App IDs (dedicated server, NOT the game client) / install method:
 *   arkasa        2430930  (ARK: Survival Ascended Dedicated Server — Windows-only, Wine/Proton-GE image)
 *   soulmask      3017300  (Soulmask Dedicated Server, Linux build — native Linux)
 *   dst           343050   (Don't Starve Together Dedicated Server — native Linux)
 *   vintagestory  N/A      (NOT Steam-distributed — official tar.gz from vintagestory.at; .NET 8 runtime)
 *   necesse       1169370  (Necesse Dedicated Server — native Linux/cross-platform JAR)
 *   tf2           232250   (Team Fortress 2 Dedicated Server — native Linux, Source engine)
 *   l4d2          222860   (Left 4 Dead 2 Dedicated Server — native Linux, Source engine)
 *
 * Docker images picked to match publishers ALREADY trusted elsewhere in this
 * catalog where possible: indifferentbroccoli (already projectzomboid +
 * dragonwilds). tf2/l4d2 continue the cs2 precedent (prisma/catalog.ts uses
 * joedwards32/cs2) of a widely-used Source-dedicated-server publisher — TF2
 * uses cm2network (100K+ pulls, updated 7 months ago, the standard choice for
 * Source-engine TF2 containers); no equivalently-maintained single publisher
 * covers both TF2 and L4D2, so L4D2 uses left4devops/l4d2 (10K-50K pulls,
 * updated within the last several months) instead. arkasa uses sknnr's
 * Proton-GE-wrapped image, the same Wine-wrapping approach already used for
 * sunkenland/icarus/abioticfactor in Wave 3 (ASA has no official Linux build).
 * dst uses yeetzone/dontstarvetogether — env-var driven (TOKEN/NAME/PASSWORD/
 * MAX_PLAYERS), matching this platform's docker-run-driven config pattern far
 * better than the more actively-maintained but config-file-only alternatives
 * (mathielo/dst-dedicated-server, jamesits/dst-server). vintagestory uses
 * ich777/vintagestory, the standard community image (handles the non-Steam
 * tar.gz download + .NET runtime itself). necesse uses andreasgl4ser's image
 * (env-var driven, actively updated).
 *
 * Customer-specific values with no sane platform default (same precedent as
 * Wave 3's Dragonwilds OWNER_ID): DST's cluster TOKEN (Klei account-bound,
 * required for the server to run publicly at all) and TF2's SRCDS_TOKEN GSLT
 * (Steam account-bound, required to be listed & reachable). Both are seeded
 * blank in the setupScript and surfaced as real deploy-time fields in
 * lib/game-config.ts (DST.TOKEN, TF2.SRCDS_TOKEN) so the customer has an
 * actual place to set them post-order, unlike Dragonwilds' OWNER_ID which has
 * no config-schema field at all yet.
 *
 * RCON: all seven ship with rcon:"none" in lib/game-control.ts even though
 * tf2/l4d2/soulmask do have a real Source-style console underneath — mirrors
 * Wave 3's own precedent of not reverse-engineering a brand-new community
 * image's internal cfg-file layout without a live box to confirm paths
 * against. Can be upgraded to rcon:"source" later once verified live.
 *
 * NOTE: static in-container placeholder passwords ("changeme12"/blank) —
 * customers change them post-deploy, matching every prior wave.
 *
 * Run: cd /opt/nxeon-staging && npx tsx prisma/seed-wave4-games.ts   (idempotent)
 */
